{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Natural World"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Visiting the Sharks"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_9", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "massive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very large "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some sharks are massive!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about nature."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "great white shark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large species of shark"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It must be terrifying diving with a great white shark."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "too close for comfort"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dangerously or uncomfortably near"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Diving with sharks sounds too close for comfort."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tempt (a person or an animal) to do something or to go somewhere, especially by offering some form of reward"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People get in a cage and go down under the water as people on the surface lure the sharks to the area. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "element"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "natural environment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The sharks are in their element there - the humans are not! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put yourself through "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to expose yourself to a difficult or dangerous situation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must love nature to put yourself through that. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "voluntarily"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "To do something by choice "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would never voluntarily dive with sharks!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " obsessed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having something occupy your mind most of the time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must be really obsessed with nature."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "creepy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "scary "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It sounds really creepy, but interesting! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob06aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Clarification and Emphasizing a Point"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You ask for clarification when you want more details of what the other person is talking about.<br/>You can emphasize a point by asking rhetorical questions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions </span> to ask for clarification. An <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span> is a question inside another question or statement. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"strong\">Direct question:</span> <span class=\"italic\"> What was the show about sharks?</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question:</span> <span class=\"italic\"> Do you remember what that show was you watched about the sharks?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for an explanation on how to make embedded questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">rhetorical questions</span> to emphasize a point. Rhetorical questions are questions that don't have an answer. The speaker just wants to make a point about something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Do you know how many people have been killed by sharks? </span> (The speaker knows doesn't really expect the listener to tell her how many people have been killed by sharks. Rather, she wants to emphasize the point that sharks are dangerous)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you remember what that show was you watched about the sharks?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you know how many people have been killed by sharks? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you mean to tell me that they go in the water? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Showing That You Understand Someone's Feelings"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> followed by an adjective when you want to empathize with someone. When you empathize with someone, you show them that you understand their feelings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is the structure to follow:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + must + verb + adjective"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You must feel depressed.<br/> You must be excited.<br/> They must be shocked! <br/> It must be terrifying to do that!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use either <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> adjectives or <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> adjectives. <br>An adjective that ends in -ING is used to describe the characteristic of a person, a thing or a situation. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">This is a very interesting topic.</span> <br> <br> An adjective that ends in -ED is used to describe a feeling or an emotion. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\"> I was bored at the concert.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare the difference: "}, {"type": "example", "content": " You must be obsessed with nature to put yourself through that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Diving with sharks must be terrifying!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">He is bored. </span> ( It means that the person is not getting fun at the moment). <br />  <span class=\"italic\">He is boring. </span> ( It means that the person is tedious and make other people get bored)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Don't forget to include the verb before the adjective."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le12ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the activity of diving with sharks with your partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the advantages and disadvantages of doing an activity like diving with sharks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Keep the conversation going by asking follow-up questions."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the topic of diving with sharks with my partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We keep the conversation going and show understanding of someone's feelings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for clarification and emphasize a point."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can talk about nature and the animal world. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "co